*Measurement probabilities:* The probability of measuring a spin state $|psi chevron.r$ in a particular eigenstate $|phi chevron.r$ is given by the Born rule $P = |chevron.l phi | psi chevron.r|^2$. For spin-1/2 projections along axes separated by an angle $theta$, this relates to the projection angle.
